/*
Problem: Number of Visible People in a Queue (LC 1944)
Topic: Monotonic Stack

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Process people from right to left.

Maintain a decreasing stack of heights.

For each person:

• Every shorter person on the top of
  the stack is visible because the
  current person can see over them.

• Pop each shorter person and
  increase the visible count.

• If a taller (or equal) person still
  remains on the stack, that person is
  also visible, but blocks everyone
  behind them.

Finally, push the current person's
height onto the stack.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Traverse from right to left.

2. While the stack top is shorter than
   the current height:

   • Pop it.

   • Increase visible count.

3. If stack is still not empty,
   increase count by one because the
   first taller/equal person is also
   visible.

4. Push current height.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

heights = [10,6,8,5,11,9]

Process from right:

9

↓

11 sees 9

↓

5 sees 11

↓

8 sees 5 and 11

↓

6 sees 8

↓

10 sees 6, 8 and 11

Answer:

[3,1,2,1,1,0]

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The stack always stores heights in
decreasing order.

Shorter people are removed because
they are completely visible.

The first remaining taller (or equal)
person is also visible, but blocks the
view of everyone behind them.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Each person is pushed and popped at
most once.

Space : O(n)

Stack stores at most n heights.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Monotonic Decreasing Stack
*/

class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> canSeePersonsCount(vector<int>& heights) {

        int n = heights.size();

        if (n == 0)
            return {};

        stack<int> st;
        vector<int> ans(n, 0);

        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {

            // Current person sees all shorter people
            while (!st.empty() &&
                   st.top() < heights[i]) {

                ans[i]++;
                st.pop();
            }

            // First taller/equal person is also visible
            if (!st.empty()) {
                ans[i]++;
            }

            st.push(heights[i]);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
